    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always seen math as a tool to understand the world, especially in physics and engineering. While I’m not a mathematician, I find it fascinating how patterns and logic shape reality. I enjoy solving problems, especially those with real-world applications. My parents’ background—my dad with a PhD and my mom with only primary education—also taught me that math isn’t about perfection, but about curiosity and persistence.",
